					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-4060713#post-3619810</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-4060713/scp-029-j#post-3619810</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 25 Oct 2017 17:44:44 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Weryllium</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2727655</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I'm kinda ambivalent on this. &quot;Jesus as an Uber driver&quot; is a decent premise but I feel like you stretched it out way too thin and long here. There are some bits that I personally really love (&quot;did you actually just ask God how he knows something?&quot;, &quot;Wait this is voluntary?&quot;) and then some bits that kill it for me again (the corgis in particular, because I've gotten so sick of 'lol corgi'). It ends up being the literary equivalent of a big bag of cheap trail mix, so I'm gonna leave it neutral for now. I don't hate it, but I don't particularly love it either.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
